  "term": "stress hormone",
  "definition": "A stress hormone is a body chemical released as part of the stress response, especially when the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis is activated. In the source, cortisol is the main example, and adrenaline is also described as a stress hormone that can affect immune activity.",
